 3. ChatGPT traffic rebounds as rivals gain ground 
 
 By Sara Fischer and Kerry Flynn 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Similarweb; Chart: Erin Davis/Axios ChatGPT's web traffic rebounded over the past three months after a volatile first half of 2026, according to Similarweb data.

 Why it matters: ChatGPT remains the leading AI chatbot by website visits even as competitors erode its market share.

 The summer rebound coincided with Google's Gemini seeing its first traffic slowdown in nearly a year and a half. Zoom in: September was ChatGPT's strongest month since October 2025 in terms of visits, per Similarweb. 

 As of last month, ChatGPT accounted for 57% of visits to eight of the world's largest AI platforms tracked by Similarweb. Similarweb's analysis does not include visits to Google's AI Overviews, which are difficult to isolate from traditional searches. The intrigue: It's unclear why visits surged for ChatGPT in September, while Gemini and Claude did not see similar gains. Back-to-school season could be a factor, considering Claude's largely enterprise client user base. 

 ChatGPT's dip earlier this year coincided with major marketing and product expansion efforts from Anthropic and Google. Zoom out: While ChatGPT's website visits have fluctuated, app engagement remains strong. 

